      "excerpt": "From Idea to Sustainable Growth 🚀 12 business terms every founder should understand: 1. Revenue Stream — How your business makes money. 2. MVP — The simplest version used to test market demand. 3. Revenue — To",
      "content": "From Idea to Sustainable Growth 🚀\n\n12 business terms every founder should understand:\n\n1. Revenue Stream — How your business makes money.\n2. MVP — The simplest version used to test market demand.\n3. Revenue — Total income generated from sales.\n4. Gross Profit — Revenue minus direct costs.\n5. Gross Margin — Gross profit as a % of revenue.\n6. Net Profit — What remains after all expenses.\n7. Profit Margin — Net profit as a % of revenue.\n8. Break-Even — When revenue equals total costs.\n9. Cash Flow — Cash moving in and out of the business.\n10. Burn Rate — How quickly the business spends its cash.\n11. CAC — Cost of acquiring one customer.\n12. LTV — Value generated by a customer over their lifetime.\n\nThe journey:\n\nIdea → MVP → Revenue → Profitability → Cash Management → Customer Economics → Sustainable Growth 📈\n\nRemember:\n\nRevenue ≠ Profit ≠ Cash\n\nAnd for sustainable customer acquisition:\n\nLTV > CAC\n\nA great idea can start a business.\nUnderstanding the numbers helps you build one that lasts.\n\nSave this framework. 📌",
