      "title": "Business Model vs. Business Model Canvas",
      "slug": "business-model-vs-business-model-canvas",
      "excerpt": "Business Model vs. Business Model Canvas: What’s the Difference? These two terms are often used as if they mean the same thing. They don’t. Business Model A Business Model explains how a company creates, delive",
      "content": "Business Model vs. Business Model Canvas: What’s the Difference?\n\nThese two terms are often used as if they mean the same thing.\n\nThey don’t.\n\nBusiness Model\n\nA Business Model explains how a company creates, delivers, and captures value.\n\nIt answers questions like:\n\n• Who is the customer?\n• What value do we offer?\n• How do we deliver it?\n• How does the business make money?\n• What does it cost to operate?\n\nExamples include:\n\nSubscription | Marketplace | SaaS | Freemium | Commission | Direct-to-Consumer\n\nSimply:\n\nBusiness Model = How the business works.\n\nBusiness Model Canvas\n\nThe Business Model Canvas (BMC) is a strategic tool used to visualize your business model on one page.\n\nIt contains 9 building blocks:\n\n1. Customer Segments\n2. Value Propositions\n3. Channels\n4. Customer Relationships\n5. Revenue Streams\n6. Key Resources\n7. Key Activities\n8. Key Partners\n9. Cost Structure\n\nSimply:\n\nBusiness Model Canvas = A map of how the business works.\n\nSo, what’s the difference?\n\nBusiness Model = The System\nBusiness Model Canvas = The Map\n\nThe Canvas doesn’t replace your business model — it helps you understand, structure, test, and improve it.\n\nAnd when starting a business, the journey could look like this:\n\nIdea → Problem → Customer → Value Proposition → Business Model → Business Model Canvas → MVP → Validation → Growth\n\nA good idea tells you what to build.\n\nA strong business model explains how that idea can create value and become sustainable.",
