      "title": "Trade vs. E-Commerce vs. Dropshipping vs. Marketplace",
      "slug": "trade-ecommerce-dropshipping-marketplace",
      "excerpt": "Trade vs. E-Commerce vs. Dropshipping vs. Marketplace Many entrepreneurs confuse these terms. They are connected — but they are not the same business model. Trade The broad concept of buying and selling goods o",
      "content": "Trade vs. E-Commerce vs. Dropshipping vs. Marketplace\n\nMany entrepreneurs confuse these terms.\n\nThey are connected — but they are not the same business model.\n\nTrade\nThe broad concept of buying and selling goods or services for profit.\nBuy → Sell → Margin\n\nE-Commerce\nTrade conducted through digital channels. You may own inventory, manage fulfillment, and sell directly to customers.\nInventory → Online Store → Customer\n\nDropshipping\nAn e-commerce model where you sell without holding inventory. When a customer orders, the supplier fulfills the order directly.\nCustomer → Your Store → Supplier → Customer\n\nMarketplace\nA platform that connects multiple sellers with buyers and typically earns through commissions, fees, or related services.\nSellers ↔ Platform ↔ Customers\n\nThe key difference is who owns the inventory, who fulfills the order, and how the business makes money.\n\nBefore choosing a model, ask:\n\nCapital → Inventory → Control → Margin → Risk → Scalability\n\nDon’t choose a business model because it’s trending.\n\nChoose the model that fits your market, customer, resources, and competitive advantage.",
