      "excerpt": "Organizational structure is not bureaucracy. It is the operating system of a growing business. A clear structure defines: • Who owns each function • Who makes which decisions • Who is accountable for results • ",
      "content": "Organizational structure is not bureaucracy.\n\nIt is the operating system of a growing business.\n\nA clear structure defines:\n• Who owns each function\n• Who makes which decisions\n• Who is accountable for results\n• How teams communicate\n• Where issues should be escalated\n• Which KPIs belong to each role\n\nWithout structure, growth often creates:\nDuplicate work → Slow decisions → Internal conflict → Missed accountability → Founder or manager bottlenecks.\n\nA practical sequence:\n\nStrategy → Functions → Roles → Responsibilities → Decision Rights → KPIs → Reporting Lines → Review\n\nThe goal is not to create more titles.\nThe goal is to create clarity.\n\nA strong organizational structure helps people move faster because everyone understands where they fit, what they own, and how success is measured.",
