      "excerpt": "Who is your customer? “Everyone” is usually not a useful answer. Strong businesses define their Ideal Customer Profile around: • Need — Who has the problem? • Ability — Who can afford the solution? • Authority ",
      "content": "Who is your customer?\n\n“Everyone” is usually not a useful answer.\n\nStrong businesses define their Ideal Customer Profile around:\n• Need — Who has the problem?\n• Ability — Who can afford the solution?\n• Authority — Who makes the decision?\n• Urgency — Who needs it now?\n• Fit — Who receives the most value?\n\nFor B2B, also consider industry, company size, geography, buying process, and decision-makers.\n\nBetter targeting improves your message, offer, acquisition cost, and conversion.\n\nKnow the customer before trying to scale the customer base.",
