      "excerpt": "How do you get a commercial agency or distribution agreement for an international brand? It starts long before signing the contract. 1. Research and identify brands Look for brands that fit your market, custome",
      "content": "How do you get a commercial agency or distribution agreement for an international brand?\n\nIt starts long before signing the contract.\n\n1. Research and identify brands\nLook for brands that fit your market, customers, capabilities, and portfolio.\n\n2. Prepare your company profile\nShow your market knowledge, distribution network, sales capabilities, logistics, financial capacity, and marketing strength.\n\n3. Approach the brand\nPresent a clear market opportunity and explain how your company can grow the brand locally.\n\n4. Discuss and negotiate\nDefine the model, territory, exclusivity, product range, pricing, targets, marketing support, inventory responsibilities, and after-sales service.\n\n5. Sign and start operating\nBuild the supply chain, execute the go-to-market plan, measure performance, and develop the partnership.\n\nBrands are not only looking for someone who can buy products.\nThey are looking for a partner capable of building the brand and growing market share.",
