      "title": "Exclusive vs. Non-Exclusive Distribution",
      "slug": "exclusive-vs-non-exclusive-distribution",
      "excerpt": "Exclusive vs. Non-Exclusive Distribution: which model fits your business? An exclusive distribution agreement generally gives one distributor defined rights within an agreed territory, market, product range, or",
      "content": "Exclusive vs. Non-Exclusive Distribution: which model fits your business?\n\nAn exclusive distribution agreement generally gives one distributor defined rights within an agreed territory, market, product range, or channel.\n\nThis can create:\n• Stronger distributor commitment\n• Greater brand focus\n• Clearer channel control\n• Higher investment expectations\n• More demanding sales targets\n\nNon-exclusive distribution allows a brand to work with multiple distributors within the same market.\n\nThis can create:\n• Wider market coverage\n• Faster channel expansion\n• Lower dependency on one partner\n• More competition between distributors\n• Greater flexibility when testing a market\n\nNeither model is automatically better.\n\nBefore choosing, evaluate:\nMarket size → Brand strategy → Investment capacity → Sales targets → Territory → Channel coverage → Support requirements → Long-term objectives.\n\nAnd remember: exclusivity is defined by the agreement. Territory, products, channels, performance requirements, duration, and termination conditions should be clearly documented.",
