      "excerpt": "MVP does not mean “cheap product.” A Minimum Viable Product is the simplest version of a solution that allows you to test a meaningful business assumption with real users. The goal is learning. Build → Test → M",
      "content": "MVP does not mean “cheap product.”\n\nA Minimum Viable Product is the simplest version of a solution that allows you to test a meaningful business assumption with real users.\n\nThe goal is learning.\n\nBuild → Test → Measure → Learn → Improve.\n\nA useful MVP should help answer:\n• Does the problem really exist?\n• Will customers use the solution?\n• Will they pay?\n• Which features actually matter?\n• What should we change before scaling?\n\nDon’t spend months perfecting something the market has never validated.",
