      "title": "Revenue Streams: Where Does Your Business Actually Make Money?",
      "slug": "revenue-streams-strategy",
      "excerpt": "Where does your business actually make its money? It sounds like a simple question but many businesses do not have a clear answer They know what they sell and they know their monthly sales but when you look dee",
      "content": "Where does your business actually make its money?\n\nIt sounds like a simple question but many businesses do not have a clear answer\n\nThey know what they sell and they know their monthly sales but when you look deeper you may find that one product one customer segment or one sales channel is responsible for most of the revenue\n\nThis is why understanding revenue streams matters\n\nA contractor may generate revenue from projects and maintenance contracts\n\nA software company may combine subscriptions with implementation and support services\n\nA marketplace may earn a commission from every transaction\n\nA distributor may generate most of its revenue from product sales while also earning from delivery services or additional solutions\n\nThere is no revenue model that works for every business\n\nThe important questions are simple\n\nWho pays you\n\nWhat are they paying for\n\nHow often do they pay\n\nHow much does it cost you to generate that revenue\n\nAnd how much do you actually keep\n\nAs the business grows another question becomes important\n\nAre you building stronger revenue streams or becoming more dependent on one source of income\n\nA healthy revenue strategy is not about creating as many income sources as possible\n\nIt is about understanding which revenue streams make sense for your customers and your business and which ones can continue to grow profitably over time\n\nBusiness Owner",
