    {
      "id": "article-company-exit-strategy",
      "type": "article",
      "lang": "en",
      "status": "published",
      "category": "Strategy",
      "title": "Exit Strategy: Build a Company Someone Else Would Want to Own",
      "slug": "company-exit-strategy",
      "excerpt": "A successful company exit does not begin when an offer arrives It begins years earlier Many business owners spend years building revenue customers and market presence but never ask a simple question Could this ",
      "content": "A successful company exit does not begin when an offer arrives\n\nIt begins years earlier\n\nMany business owners spend years building revenue customers and market presence but never ask a simple question\n\nCould this company continue to perform without me\n\nThat question matters because buyers are not only buying current sales\n\nThey are buying a business they believe can continue creating value after ownership changes\n\nA company becomes more attractive when its financials are clear its customer base is healthy its processes are documented and important decisions do not depend on one person\n\nThe same applies to management\n\nIf every major relationship approval and operational decision still requires the owner then the buyer is not acquiring an independent business\n\nThey are acquiring a business that still depends on its founder\n\nPreparing for an exit therefore means building transferable value\n\nStrong management\n\nReliable financial reporting\n\nDocumented operations\n\nRecurring or predictable revenue\n\nHealthy margins\n\nLow customer concentration\n\nClear contracts and ownership of intellectual property\n\nAn exit can take different forms\n\nA strategic acquisition\n\nA management buyout\n\nA sale to an investor\n\nA merger\n\nOr a gradual transfer of ownership\n\nThe right option depends on what the owner wants from the next stage and what the business is actually worth to a buyer\n\nThe best time to think about an exit is not when you want to leave\n\nIt is while you still have time to build a company someone else would want to own\n\nBusiness Owner",
      "featured_image": "",
      "author": "Business Owner",
