      "slug": "cac-ltv-customer-economics",
      "excerpt": "Growth is expensive when customer economics are ignored. Two metrics every growing business should understand: CAC — Customer Acquisition Cost: How much does it cost to acquire a customer? LTV — Customer Lifeti",
      "content": "Growth is expensive when customer economics are ignored.\n\nTwo metrics every growing business should understand:\n\nCAC — Customer Acquisition Cost:\nHow much does it cost to acquire a customer?\n\nLTV — Customer Lifetime Value:\nHow much value does that customer generate over the relationship?\n\nA healthy business needs customer value to justify acquisition cost. But LTV > CAC is only the beginning.\n\nAlso watch:\n• Gross margin\n• Retention\n• Payback period\n• Repeat purchase rate\n• Churn\n\nMore customers do not automatically mean a healthier business.",
